.TH "SOPLOS-KERNEL-INSTALLER" "1" "2026-11-17" "Soplos Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
soplos-kernel-installer \- Build and install Linux kernels on Soplos Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B soplos-kernel-installer
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B soplos-kernel-installer
builds and installs Linux kernels on Soplos Linux. Built with Tauri 2, Rust and
Svelte, it is organized in four pages and a hidden fifth one:
.IP \[bu] 2
.B Build:
an assistant that asks what the computer is for, which kernel is wanted (the
newest stable one, a long-term one, or a release candidate to help to test),
what the computer is like and, at the end, shows a recipe that can be edited
before the build. It downloads the kernel from kernel.org and checks it against
the published hash, applies the patches, configures the kernel, compiles it in
.I ~/kernel_build
and installs it. A build goes on while the page is left, and can be cancelled.
.IP \[bu]
.B Kernels:
installs and removes the ready-made kernels of Soplos, Debian (standard and
real-time), XanMod and Liquorix, each with its own repository.
.IP \[bu]
.B Installed:
lists the kernels found in
.I /boot
and removes the ones that are not running.
.IP \[bu]
.B Secure Boot:
a step by step guide: it detects the bootloader (GRUB, systemd-boot or Limine),
creates a key, makes the firmware trust it, signs kernels and bootloaders, and
checks the whole chain before Secure Boot is turned on.
.IP \[bu]
.B Batch
(hidden, shown with Ctrl+Shift+D): builds a whole release of kernels of
Soplos, one after another, into a folder that is chosen.
.P
The interface is available in English, Spanish, German, French, Italian,
Portuguese, Romanian and Russian. It starts in the system language and falls
back to English.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B F1
About.
.TP
.B Ctrl+1 to Ctrl+4
Build, Kernels, Installed and Secure Boot.
.TP
.B Ctrl+5
Batch, when it is shown.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Tab, Ctrl+Shift+Tab
The next page and the previous page.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+D
Shows or hides the Batch page.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quits.
.SH SECURITY
The window never runs as root. What needs the administrator is asked as named
operations, under one polkit action,
.IR org.soplos.kernelinstaller.run-privileged ,
and the program checks each one again as root. The password of the firmware, when
a key is enrolled, goes through the standard input of the administrator step and
never touches a file.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/kernel_build
The sources, the patches, the log (build.log) and the packages of the builds.
.TP
.I ~/.config/soplos-kernel-installer/keys
The key of the user for Secure Boot. The private half never leaves the computer.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/soplos-kernel-installer/history.json
The kernels built with the program.
.TP
.I /var/lib/soplos-kernel-installer
A copy of the key that only root can read, kept while the automatic signing is on.
.TP
.I /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/99soplos-kernel-installer-sign
The hook that signs again, after every update, what was left without a signature.
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/org.soplos.kernelinstaller.policy
The polkit action of the program.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt (8),
.BR dkms (8),
.BR mokutil (1),
.BR sbsign (1),
.BR pkexec (1)
